# Unit VI - Pranayama & Breathing Practices
INTRO_U6 = {
 "about": "<b>Pranayama</b> = <i>Prana</i> (vital life force) + <i>Ayama</i> (expansion / regulation): regulating, becoming aware of, and controlling the breath. It builds awareness of breathing patterns, concentration, relaxation, and physical-mental balance. Different techniques give relaxing, cooling, balancing, controlled or energising effects. You must know the technique, breathing pattern, benefits and precautions of each prescribed practice and demonstrate it correctly in the practical exam.",
 "guidelines": [
  "Clean, quiet, well-ventilated place",
  "Sit steadily — Sukhasana, Padmasana, Vajrasana or another stable seat — spine upright",
  "Relax shoulders, face and abdomen (unless a technique needs controlled muscle use)",
  "Empty or light stomach, preferably before meals",
  "Breathe gently and naturally — never force or strain",
  "Beginners: no long breath retention unless taught and supervised by a qualified instructor",
  "Stop at once for dizziness, chest discomfort, unusual breathlessness or discomfort",
  "Asthma, significant respiratory/cardiovascular conditions, uncontrolled blood pressure or other concerns → medical advice before forceful or specialised techniques",
 ],
}

